1
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:05,190
For the first time in history, two teams

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,440
Nankatsu and Toho Academy

3
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:12,240
have jointly won the Middle School Tournament.

4
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:17,490
Nankatsu

5
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:17,490
Toho

6
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:17,490
16th Middle School Football Tournament

7
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,490
Archrivals

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,620
Ozora Tsubasa and Kojiro Hyuga

9
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:22,580
and the selected members

10
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:26,330
are stepping onto the world stage for the first time.

11
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:30,050
Tsubasa now thinks about the big matches awaiting him.

12
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:34,380
- Come on, faster!
- Get your foot in!

13
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:41,520
Too weak!

14
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:46,650
Y-you...

15
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,230
Karl Heinz Schneider

16
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:55,530
I officially joined Munich.

17
00:00:55,910 --> 00:00:58,280
So you're leaving Hamburg for Munich?

18
00:00:58,570 --> 00:00:59,660
Impossible!

19
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:02,580
You're the number one product of Hamburg's youth system.

20
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,540
You've been here since childhood!

21
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:08,040
Striker Schneider and the impenetrable goalkeeper Wakabayashi

22
00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:10,590
You two made Hamburg

23
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:13,800
an unbeatable team in the youth category.

24
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,930
Thanks to the two of you

25
00:01:16,050 --> 00:01:18,800
we won every single trophy

26
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:20,850
in Germany and Europe this season.

27
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:23,720
You're betraying Hamburg!

28
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:25,180
It's very simple.

29
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:29,060
Munich values its captain more.

30
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:33,440
They want me to play for them in the Bundesliga next season.

31
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:36,320
Wherever I go, I'll give it my all.

32
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:40,780
My jersey may have changed but I'm still the same.

33
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:43,410
I have only one goal:

34
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:45,700
To be stronger than everyone else.

35
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:47,580
and to be number one.

36
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:52,340
I won't settle for anything less than becoming the best player in the world.

37
00:01:53,630 --> 00:01:55,460
I share the same ambition.

38
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,970
Let's have our final duel, Wakabayashi.

39
00:02:02,470 --> 00:02:03,560
It's my honour.

40
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:08,270
From outside the penalty area, right?

41
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:09,480
Yes.

42
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,570
The talented goalkeeper, Genzo Wakabayashi...

43
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:13,730
This season

44
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:18,740
has not conceded a single goal from outside the box.

45
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:20,490
In this final duel,

46
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:24,120
will Schneider be able to break through that wall?

47
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:26,500
Get ready, Wakabayashi!

48
00:02:26,910 --> 00:02:27,750
I'm ready!

49
00:02:49,350 --> 00:02:52,270
JUNIOR YOUTH

50
00:02:49,350 --> 00:02:52,270
SEASON 2

51
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:16,980
EPISODE 1 A NEW CHALLENGE

52
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:20,730
Shizuoka Training Ground - Japan U-15 Team

53
00:04:33,410 --> 00:04:35,420
In these three days of training

54
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:37,960
we can truly feel their excitement.

55
00:04:38,090 --> 00:04:38,960
Yes.

56
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:45,090
This camp is in preparation for the France U-15 Tournament

57
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:46,640
and in general

58
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:50,010
organized to strengthen ourselves against major national teams.

59
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,310
Right.

60
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:56,400
Urgently, we must select the main squad for the upcoming matches.

61
00:04:56,650 --> 00:04:59,480
Misugi-kun, you too, as an assistant coach...

62
00:04:59,610 --> 00:05:04,280
You should observe the training sessions and suggest a squad to me.

63
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:05,400
Understood.

64
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:07,360
Alright, that's enough running.

65
00:05:07,490 --> 00:05:08,410
Yes, sir!

66
00:05:13,370 --> 00:05:15,160
Actually, this team

67
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,250
has many good players.

68
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:18,920
Just

69
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:21,250
one thing is missing.

70
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:22,800
Clearly.

71
00:05:23,090 --> 00:05:25,920
Tsubasa-kun's absence is intensely felt.

72
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:30,050
With him setting up play and looking for goals,

73
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:32,770
the team will be incredibly strong.

74
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:37,440
Today I've become completely convinced of that.

75
00:05:38,770 --> 00:05:42,730
But Tsubasa-kun is at home in recovery.

76
00:05:43,070 --> 00:05:47,570
Ozora

77
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:46,990
I think we'll have to say goodbye to the European tournament.

78
00:05:48,070 --> 00:05:50,740
Now, read these sentences.

79
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:53,910
Sorry for interrupting.

80
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,580
You're welcome.

81
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:58,040
Well done Tsubasa, you pronounced it very well.

82
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,290
I'm tired.

83
00:06:00,790 --> 00:06:03,840
Carlos, shall we rest a bit?

84
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:05,340
No, you can't!

85
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:09,680
Once your injury heals, you'll return to football.

86
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:12,550
Now it's time to study.

87
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:16,020
Now write this sentence in your notebook.

88
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:17,310
Okay.

89
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:19,020
Ryo Ishizaki

90
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:21,110
Carlos, give me a minute.

91
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,820
Ishizaki-kun sent a video.

92
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:31,570
Ishizaki

93
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:27,030
Tsubasa, you're our ball buddy!

94
00:06:27,150 --> 00:06:29,530
We're getting ready for a match.

95
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,660
We're waiting for you to play with us again, we miss you!

96
00:06:33,030 --> 00:06:35,490
Guys, come here, hurry up!

97
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:44,710
Ishizaki

98
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:37,580
I'm sending this to Tsubasa.

99
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:38,790
Did you say Tsubasa?

100
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:42,080
Tsubasa, join us quickly.

101
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,710
Hyuga and I are waiting for you.

102
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:46,550
Matsuyama-kun!

103
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:51,720
After this camp we're flying to Europe.

104
00:06:52,550 --> 00:06:54,220
I would like to go there too.

105
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:56,470
During that trip

106
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:59,600
maybe I can see Misaki-kun and Wakabayashi-kun again.

107
00:06:59,730 --> 00:07:01,810
You're lucky, Tsubasa.

108
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:04,860
You have many friends.

109
00:07:05,070 --> 00:07:05,900
Yes!

110
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:09,240
I've known them since elementary school.

111
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:13,740
When I came to live here, my first friend was Ishizaki-kun.

112
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:24,170
Then I saw Wakabayashi-kun.

113
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:27,500
What connected us was football.

114
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:30,170
Is that really Wakabayashi?

115
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:32,300
He's in Germany, isn't he?

116
00:07:32,430 --> 00:07:34,930
Yes! A legendary goalkeeper.

117
00:07:35,050 --> 00:07:38,020
He catches every shot from outside the penalty area.

118
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:40,810
Oh! He's your rival!

119
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:49,440
That's Schneider's famous fire shot from outside the box!

120
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:55,200
This reminds me of my match against Tsubasa in elementary school.

121
00:07:56,160 --> 00:08:00,450
Back then, I caught every shot from outside the penalty area.

122
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,750
Tsubasa was the only one

123
00:08:02,870 --> 00:08:05,710
who ended the invincibility I took pride in.

124
00:08:08,130 --> 00:08:10,460
And now, Schneider...

125
00:08:10,710 --> 00:08:14,300
Our duels always remind me of Tsubasa.

126
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:21,890
It's a goal!

127
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,770
Schneider won the duel.

128
00:08:24,690 --> 00:08:28,110
In total, it's 50 wins, 50 losses.

129
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,940
I admit my defeat.

130
00:08:31,650 --> 00:08:34,910
The power of your shot has improved.

131
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,450
The ball accelerated near my hands.

132
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:41,660
You too, one day you'll reach the top.

133
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:46,210
And on that day, we'll know for good who is better, Wakabayashi.

134
00:08:48,210 --> 00:08:50,170
When are you going to Munich?

135
00:08:50,590 --> 00:08:52,380
Before I put it on,

136
00:08:52,970 --> 00:08:55,430
I won't leave without wearing the Hamburg jersey one last time.

137
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:58,550
Do you understand what that means?

138
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:03,640
Mikami-san promised me that Japan's team

139
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:07,060
would play its first match in Europe here, against Hamburg.

140
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:10,730
That will be their first match in Europe.

141
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:14,490
They'll see the progress I've made in Germany.

142
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:16,860
Hello, Tsubasa

143
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:20,200
We come bearing good news, how's your injury?

144
00:09:20,330 --> 00:09:21,330
Guys!

145
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:23,660
Tsubasa-senpai, this is for you.

146
00:09:23,790 --> 00:09:24,870
Thank you.

147
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:28,710
Actually, the idea to visit you came from Kumi-chan.

148
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:32,630
Good thing, you don't need to worry.

149
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:36,090
Look at my shoulder, my foot is almost healed too.

150
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,970
Luckily the bones and tendons are intact.

151
00:09:39,090 --> 00:09:42,640
After those rough moves in the national tournament...

152
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:46,230
Do you think you're indestructible?

153
00:09:46,850 --> 00:09:49,690
Thanks to my parents, I grew up this strong.

154
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:53,820
Tsubasa, don't your feet itch to kick a ball?

155
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:56,820
Yes! I'll be back soon.

156
00:09:57,070 --> 00:09:59,200
No, Tsubasa-kun! Be sensible.

157
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,950
Yes, senpai.

158
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:03,200
Don't train until you're completely recovered.

159
00:10:03,330 --> 00:10:04,330
They're right.

160
00:10:04,450 --> 00:10:07,580
For now, focus on your Portuguese.

161
00:10:08,670 --> 00:10:09,790
Right.

162
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:13,590
You're going to Brazil next year.

163
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:15,130
Hmm.

164
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,480
Coach.

165
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:32,980
Here is the squad I designed.

166
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:34,980
I see.

167
00:10:35,110 --> 00:10:38,240
It's almost exactly like my selection.

168
00:10:38,990 --> 00:10:43,450
But it's odd that you placed Matsuyama-kun behind the defense.

169
00:10:43,830 --> 00:10:44,660
Yes.

170
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:49,330
To build a strong midfield stretching from the goal to center forward.

171
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:53,250
A defensive midfielder and his protectors are needed.

172
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:57,760
Of course, if Tsubasa-kun is in the squad.

173
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,760
Yes, and Genzo is also missing.

174
00:11:02,470 --> 00:11:04,050
Wakabayashi-kun?

175
00:11:04,850 --> 00:11:07,390
If he returns from Germany

176
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:09,640
our defense will be more solid than ever.

177
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:17,230
What is it, Kumi-cha...

178
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:18,740
Nakazawa-senpai

179
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:22,530
What do you think about Tsubasa-senpai?

180
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,490
I

181
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:27,290
I like Tsubasa-senpai very much.

182
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,580
At first I admired senpai.

183
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:35,630
But without realizing it, I fell in love.

184
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:39,380
Before he goes to Brazil

185
00:11:39,630 --> 00:11:42,130
I want to confess my feelings to him.

186
00:11:42,930 --> 00:11:46,430
Since I love him, why should I hide it?

187
00:11:48,470 --> 00:11:50,600
Excuse me, I'm leaving.

188
00:11:56,690 --> 00:11:59,690
The next day

189
00:11:59,990 --> 00:12:02,570
Listen up. Today you'll play

190
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:06,530
against the students of Mihara High School!

191
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:09,200
Don't let your guard down!

192
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:10,330
Yes!

193
00:12:10,830 --> 00:12:12,660
Alright, let's go guys!

194
00:12:12,790 --> 00:12:13,710
Okay!

195
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:18,210
Here it is, the first match of the Japan youth team!

196
00:12:18,210 --> 00:12:21,720
Japan U-15 - Mihara High School

197
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:25,720
No mercy! We won't lose to these middle school kids!

198
00:12:34,730 --> 00:12:37,980
These high schoolers are completely dominating us.

199
00:12:38,110 --> 00:12:41,740
Yes, especially in midfield.

200
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:46,070
That's why our striker Hyuga isn't getting any balls.

201
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:54,920
It was a good idea to keep Matsuyama-kun at the back.

202
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:58,130
He's defending with incredible determination.

203
00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:01,510
Yes. With his attacking and ball-holding ability,

204
00:13:01,630 --> 00:13:03,380
he has everything a defender needs.

205
00:13:03,630 --> 00:13:04,630
I won't allow it!

206
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,130
Great clearance!

207
00:13:07,890 --> 00:13:09,430
We can never win like this...

208
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:11,470
Be a little patient, Hyuga!

209
00:13:12,890 --> 00:13:16,520
I'm the playmaker right now, leave it to me.

210
00:13:16,650 --> 00:13:19,150
Don't worry, I'll send the ball to you.

211
00:13:19,270 --> 00:13:22,110
So just stay forward.

212
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:23,190
Yes!

213
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:25,700
We won't let them get past us anymore!

214
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:27,610
We're as strong as they are!

215
00:13:28,950 --> 00:13:30,870
Yes! Matsuyama!

216
00:13:30,990 --> 00:13:33,410
Awesome! Ishizaki is unpredictable!

217
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:34,870
Keep going, Ishizaki!

218
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:37,620
Hyuga!

219
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:40,590
- Your turn!
- This counterattack, get back!

220
00:13:42,670 --> 00:13:43,760
Matsuyama...

221
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,050
Hyuga-san!

222
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:49,510
His first ball in this match!

223
00:13:52,180 --> 00:13:54,770
To find a new target for myself,

224
00:13:55,270 --> 00:13:57,850
to understand that after Toho I can become

225
00:13:58,060 --> 00:14:01,730
the star striker of the Japan U-15 team,

226
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:03,860
to measure my progress...

227
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,110
I must test myself against high schoolers...

228
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:10,740
Here's my Tiger Shot!

229
00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:17,210
Goal!

230
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:19,250
We scored the first goal!

231
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:26,010
Team

232
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:26,010
Japan

233
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:26,010
Birth

234
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:26,010
Height

235
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:26,010
Weight

236
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:26,010
Blood Type

237
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:32,140
Sanae-chan?

238
00:14:32,890 --> 00:14:36,390
Ah... well, I was just passing by...

239
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:40,650
I see... Look, I have to go meet my husband.

240
00:14:41,650 --> 00:14:44,320
Okay then, I'm going home.

241
00:14:44,610 --> 00:14:48,490
No, it's fine. You go inside, Tsubasa is upstairs in his room.

242
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:50,410
See you later, Sanae-chan.

243
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:51,820
Goodbye.

244
00:14:56,370 --> 00:14:57,580
Tsubasa-kun?

245
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:03,040
Tsubasa-kun?

246
00:15:14,430 --> 00:15:16,140
I hope you recover quickly.

247
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,560
Principal? What are you doing here?

248
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:24,440
Sorry, did I wake you?

249
00:15:25,570 --> 00:15:26,690
Where's my mom?

250
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,240
She went to meet your dad.

251
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:32,070
What? Did I sleep that late?

252
00:15:36,030 --> 00:15:37,040
What's wrong?

253
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:41,710
Tsubasa-kun...

254
00:15:44,290 --> 00:15:45,710
Tsubasa-kun

255
00:15:46,290 --> 00:15:47,210
I...

256
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:50,300
Let me turn on the light, it's gotten dark.

257
00:16:00,730 --> 00:16:05,860
Ryo Ishizaki

258
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:03,600
You have a phone call!

259
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:04,690
Excuse me...

260
00:16:07,610 --> 00:16:10,070
- Ishizaki-kun
We won, Tsubasa!

261
00:16:10,190 --> 00:16:12,280
3-1 against the high schoolers.

262
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,950
That's our team's first victory!

263
00:16:15,070 --> 00:16:18,080
Tsubasa, you should've seen it! It was the Mihara High School team.

264
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:21,250
Mihara is a prestigious team! Great job, guys!

265
00:16:21,910 --> 00:16:24,170
They beat a high school team.

266
00:16:24,370 --> 00:16:25,920
Amazing!

267
00:16:26,290 --> 00:16:27,630
Who's with you?

268
00:16:27,750 --> 00:16:29,840
Ah, the principal.

269
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:32,170
Or did I interrupt something?

270
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:33,340
What business?

271
00:16:33,590 --> 00:16:35,140
Oh, nothing...

272
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:38,760
Anyway, without you we're struggling in midfield.

273
00:16:38,890 --> 00:16:40,970
Tsubasa-san, I'm Takeshi.

274
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:44,600
Today, Hyuga-san scored all three of our goals.

275
00:16:44,850 --> 00:16:46,310
A hat-trick...

276
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:48,650
Don't let him steal the spotlight from you!

277
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,610
Looks like Hyuga-kun is in great form!

278
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:55,240
Our training camp is close to Shizuoka.

279
00:16:55,410 --> 00:16:58,370
When you can walk, come visit us.

280
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:00,160
Okay, I'll come.

281
00:17:00,370 --> 00:17:01,490
I promise.

282
00:17:01,660 --> 00:17:02,790
I'm back.

283
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,870
I'll call again later.

284
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:07,630
Tsubasa, I'm home!

285
00:17:07,830 --> 00:17:09,630
Welcome back, Dad.

286
00:17:09,880 --> 00:17:11,710
Is your foot better?

287
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:13,630
Yes, it's almost healed.

288
00:17:13,630 --> 00:17:16,180
Japan U-15 beat two high school teams!

289
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,640
They won 3-1 with total dominance in the second half!

290
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:25,640
Hello guys!

291
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:27,150
Tsubasa-kun!

292
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,060
Tsubasa!

293
00:17:29,190 --> 00:17:30,730
You can walk normally?

294
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:31,650
Yes!

295
00:17:34,740 --> 00:17:36,650
Your opponent has arrived.

296
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,030
What?

297
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:40,410
But that's...

298
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:45,040
Toho Academy, winners of the high school tournament!

299
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:48,370
A match against Toho?

300
00:17:48,630 --> 00:17:49,380
Right.

301
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,300
As I guessed, they are

302
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:55,590
more tense than in the other matches.

303
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:58,800
If we can't stand up to this team

304
00:17:58,930 --> 00:18:02,810
we won't win any match in the European tournament.

305
00:18:07,390 --> 00:18:10,110
Alright! Let's go! This time we'll score!

306
00:18:10,230 --> 00:18:11,060
Yes!

307
00:18:11,060 --> 00:18:14,070
Japan U-15 vs Toho High School warm-up match

308
00:18:14,230 --> 00:18:15,610
As I expected

309
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:19,360
the opponent controls the midfield completely.

310
00:18:19,490 --> 00:18:20,320
Right.

311
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,330
What's wrong with you bastards!

312
00:18:23,950 --> 00:18:24,950
Tsubasa-kun

313
00:18:26,040 --> 00:18:30,830
If you were in midfield, the match would be completely different.

314
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:32,840
Misugi-kun

315
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:36,590
If you were playing too, you could change the situation.

316
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:42,390
Great catch, Wakashimazu!

317
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:45,430
If I were on this field...

318
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,180
If only I could play...

319
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:51,310
Guys! Time to answer them!

320
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,360
Yes!

321
00:18:54,020 --> 00:18:55,320
I'll cover this!

322
00:18:55,690 --> 00:18:58,360
I can say right now that this is a great team.

323
00:18:58,490 --> 00:18:59,360
Right.

324
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:03,700
Each player is doing their job in their position.

325
00:19:03,990 --> 00:19:06,160
And overall, they are united.

326
00:19:06,410 --> 00:19:08,290
Attack again!

327
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:10,420
Good! Catch!

328
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:12,290
Let's go!

329
00:19:12,750 --> 00:19:14,340
With these players

330
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:17,420
this team can become number one in the world.

331
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:23,220
Despite the pressure throughout the match

332
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:26,310
goalkeeper Wakashimazu

333
00:19:26,810 --> 00:19:29,560
Jito and the others kept the defense solid.

334
00:19:29,810 --> 00:19:31,310
And in the 18th minute of the second half

335
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:33,900
thanks to Sawada's pass to Hyuga

336
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:38,570
and Matsuyama's short-range jumping volley, the match was tied.

337
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:44,820
Japan U-15 1 - Toho Academy 1

338
00:19:39,570 --> 00:19:42,530
And as the match nears its end

339
00:19:42,660 --> 00:19:44,820
the score is still 1-1.

340
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:49,160
Only 1 minute left! Play with all your strength!

341
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:50,830
You can win!

342
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,210
Tsubasa!

343
00:19:52,370 --> 00:19:54,290
Hurry! Give me the ball!

344
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:55,340
Catch!

345
00:19:56,250 --> 00:19:57,300
I'll get it!

346
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,590
- What?
- That sharp spinning pass!

347
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:03,090
He came out of Soda's area and passed to Hyuga!

348
00:20:03,970 --> 00:20:05,850
A volley shot without stopping?

349
00:20:05,970 --> 00:20:09,100
Tiger Shot!

350
00:20:14,350 --> 00:20:15,360
What?!

351
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,020
Oh yeah! We won!

352
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:18,860
Nice shot, Hyuga!

353
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:25,870
Japan U-15 Team Training Camp
Third Match

354
00:20:20,610 --> 00:20:22,030
The match is over.

355
00:20:22,150 --> 00:20:25,660
Japan U-15 wins 2-1.

356
00:20:26,030 --> 00:20:27,870
Just what you'd expect, Hyuga-kun!

357
00:20:28,370 --> 00:20:29,990
In a short time

358
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:34,210
you've made visible progress, Hyuga.

359
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:37,460
This shot has completely convinced me.

360
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:41,630
The captain of the U-15 team

361
00:20:42,170 --> 00:20:44,090
is you, Kojiro Hyuga.

362
00:20:44,550 --> 00:20:47,390
You guys were amazing! A fantastic game.

363
00:20:47,510 --> 00:20:50,270
- We won, Tsubasa!
- Three matches, three wins.

364
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:52,520
That was a nice shot, Hyuga-kun.

365
00:20:52,810 --> 00:20:53,560
Thanks.

366
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:55,350
You didn't come all the way here for nothing.

367
00:20:55,730 --> 00:20:59,360
Misugi, would you like to give it to Tsubasa?

368
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:00,280
Yes.

369
00:21:01,730 --> 00:21:02,780
This is mine?

370
00:21:02,990 --> 00:21:06,320
Everyone could choose any number they wanted.

371
00:21:06,490 --> 00:21:09,910
But no one dared take the number 10.

372
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:13,500
But I wasn't at the training camp.

373
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:18,040
Besides, Hyuga-kun and Matsuyama-kun also usually wear number 10.

374
00:21:18,210 --> 00:21:19,340
It doesn't matter.

375
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:24,220
The number 10 of Japan U-15 suits only you.

376
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:26,550
We all agree, Tsubasa.

377
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,010
Hyuga-kun...

378
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:33,060
Tsubasa, without number 10, there is no Tsubasa!

379
00:21:33,310 --> 00:21:35,560
Guys...

380
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,070
What's wrong, Tsubasa?

381
00:21:42,690 --> 00:21:46,530
Now I want to go to Europe even more.

382
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:56,830
Japan U-15 European Tournament selection meeting

383
00:21:51,330 --> 00:21:53,450
Today's Toho match

384
00:21:53,580 --> 00:21:56,660
concluded the training camp.

385
00:21:57,120 --> 00:22:00,080
For the European Tournament

386
00:22:00,250 --> 00:22:02,590
I am now announcing the list of selected members.

387
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:50,030
To be continued...

388
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:50,030
Greetings to an Old Foe